USAGE = """\
usage: scripts/config/compare --binary <blaze> [--oracle <bazel>] [--case ID]... [--label NAME]
                              [--skip-oracle]
       scripts/config/compare list
       scripts/config/compare selftest
       scripts/config/compare help

Runs a fixed list of commands (see `list`) on the probe workspace scripts/config/probe with the
oracle and with Blaze. Each side has its own copy of the workspace
(~/.cache/blaze/work/config-compare/<side>, rsync of the probe; a case may replace files of the
copy, see `files` in the case list, and they are restored after the case) and its own output
user root (~/.cache/blaze/oracle-out/config-compare-<side>), a clean environment (HOME,
PATH=/usr/bin:/bin), --nohome_rc --nosystem_rc, the shared repository cache, --color=no
--curses=no, under systemd-run --user --scope -p MemoryMax=12G -p MemorySwapMax=0. Both sides
run the same cases in the same order from a fresh output root. The oracle keeps its server
between cases (Blaze has none: audit round 3, B1).

Compared per case: the termination, the whole stdout and the whole stderr, after the exclusion
rules of scripts/lib/compare_common.py (VOLATILE_RULES; `paths`: each side's workspace copy,
output user root and output base; B1_GAP_RULES: lines that depend on the oracle's warm server,
among them its "discarding analysis cache" warning), listed in the report with the lines each
changed or removed on each side.

Guards (scripts/lib/compare_common.py): every command runs under a supervisor in the scope that
records how it really ended (`exit N`, `signal NAME`, `oom-kill`, `timeout`), and `exit` compares
those; --oracle must be the pinned oracle (sha256 in UPSTREAM.json); an empty selection is an
error. Classes per case: IDENTICAL (all of it equal after the volatile rules; the oracle exited
0, or DECLARED_EXIT declares the case's exit code as the failure under test), KNOWN-GAP (equal
except in B1 lines), DIFFERENT, BOTH-FAILED (equal failures
not declared), NOT-PORTED, ORACLE-UNEXPECTED, SKIPPED.

Output: a header (repository HEAD and dirty flag, both binaries with sha256), a table, the
denominator; raw and normalised outputs under
~/.cache/blaze/config-compare/<label>/<side>/<case>.{stdout,stderr,norm.json}, and
results.json (with the provenance and denominator). Exit 0 only when at least one case was
compared and every selected case is IDENTICAL; 1 otherwise; 2 on a usage error or a refusal.
The terminations of the `shutdown` commands are listed; one that died abnormally fails the run.
--skip-oracle reuses the oracle outputs of an earlier run with the same --label (the raw files
<label>/oracle/<case>.{stdout,stderr,json}) only when <label>/oracle/oracle.key, written after
those files were complete, holds this run's key (oracle sha256, every argv and the environment,
the digest of the probe workspace and of each case's files, the case sequence) and every file
it anchors is unchanged; otherwise it refuses. The outputs are raw (normalised when compared),
so this tool's sha256 is not in the key.
selftest drives this command line with fake binaries (compare_common.selftest_tool).
"""

